cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GeoPulse or GeoPulse-Bench, please cite it as below."
title: "GeoPulse: open-source multimodal geospatial AI for Earth-change intelligence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rahaman
    given-names: Nafiz
version: 0.5.2
date-released: 2026-10-02
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nrahaman1/geopulse"
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - earth observation
  - Sentinel-1
  - Sentinel-2
  - change detection
  - flood mapping
  - wildfire
  - forest disturbance
abstract: >-
  GeoPulse maps flood inundation, wildfire burn scars and vegetation disturbance from Sentinel-1 SAR,
  Sentinel-2 optical imagery and the Copernicus DEM. It provides STAC-based data acquisition on deterministic
  grids, training-free physics baselines, a multi-task quality-gated fusion network with calibrated uncertainty,
  event-split benchmarks with independent labels (MTBS, Hansen Global Forest Change), and a CLI, Python SDK,
  REST API and web map producing Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF, GeoJSON and STAC outputs with provenance.
